.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH rqx-check 1  "check " 
.SH NAME
rqx\-check \- Analyze changed files against a base revision and fail if the gate is not met
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrqx check\fR [\fB\-\-level\fR] [\fB\-\-base\fR] [\fB\-\-fix\fR] [\fB\-w\fR|\fB\-\-write\fR] [\fB\-\-severity\fR] [\fB\-\-rule\fR] [\fB\-\-category\fR] [\fB\-\-path\fR] [\fB\-\-not\-rule\fR] [\fB\-\-not\-category\fR] [\fB\-\-not\-path\fR] [\fB\-\-confidence\fR] [\fB\-\-fixable\fR] [\fB\-\-search\fR] [\fB\-\-since\fR] [\fB\-\-changed\fR] [\fB\-\-show\-passed\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-\-timings\fR] [\fB\-\-stats\fR] [\fB\-\-group\-by\fR] [\fB\-\-sort\fR] [\fB\-\-top\fR] [\fB\-\-show\-suppressed\fR] [\fB\-\-context\fR] [\fB\-\-detail\fR] [\fB\-\-reporter\fR] [\fB\-\-fail\-on\fR] [\fB\-\-allow\-findings\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-tui\fR] [\fB\-\-min\-health\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-mouse\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-\-min\-grade\fR] [\fB\-\-fail\-on\-incomplete\fR] [\fB\-\-motion\fR] [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-progress\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIPATH\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Analyze changed files against a base revision and fail if the gate is not met
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-level\fR \fI<LEVEL>\fR
relaxed, standard, strict or pristine
.TP
\fB\-\-base\fR \fI<BASE>\fR [default: origin/HEAD]
Revision to compare against
.TP
\fB\-\-fix\fR
Apply the mechanical fixes to what the branch touched before gating, so a branch whose only failures were mechanical passes
.TP
\fB\-w\fR, \fB\-\-write\fR
With \-\-fix, write the fixes. Without it nothing on disk changes
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-tui\fR
Never open the interactive interface; bare `rqx` prints the report instead
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-mouse\fR
Leave the mouse to the terminal. The session never captures it; the flag is still accepted so an existing invocation keeps working
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<COLOR>\fR [default: auto]
When to colour output; `auto` follows NO_COLOR and whether stdout is a terminal
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto
.IP \(bu 2
always
.IP \(bu 2
never
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-motion\fR \fI<MOTION>\fR [default: on]
Animation in the interactive interface
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
on
.IP \(bu 2
off
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Read settings from this file, layered over any `rqx.yaml` found
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-progress\fR
Do not draw the progress bar on stderr; `\-\-quiet` implies it
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
[\fIPATH\fR] [default: .]

.SH FILTERING
.TP
\fB\-\-severity\fR \fI<SEVERITY>\fR
Show only findings at or above this severity
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
info
.IP \(bu 2
warning
.IP \(bu 2
error
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-rule\fR \fI<SLUG>\fR
Show only this rule; repeatable
.TP
\fB\-\-category\fR \fI<FAMILY>\fR
Show only this smell family; repeatable
.TP
\fB\-\-path\fR \fI<GLOB>\fR
Show only findings in files matching this glob; repeatable
.TP
\fB\-\-not\-rule\fR \fI<SLUG>\fR
Hide this rule; repeatable
.TP
\fB\-\-not\-category\fR \fI<FAMILY>\fR
Hide this smell family; repeatable
.TP
\fB\-\-not\-path\fR \fI<GLOB>\fR
Hide findings in files matching this glob; repeatable
.TP
\fB\-\-confidence\fR \fI<CONFIDENCE>\fR
Show only findings rqx is certain of, or only the ones it is guessing at
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
verified
.IP \(bu 2
heuristic
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-fixable\fR
Show only findings `rqx fix` can act on
.TP
\fB\-\-search\fR \fI<TEXT>\fR
Show only findings whose rule, file or evidence contains this text
.TP
\fB\-\-since\fR \fI<REF>\fR
Show only findings in files this revision changed
.TP
\fB\-\-changed\fR
Show only findings in files not yet committed
.SH DISPLAY
.TP
\fB\-\-show\-passed\fR
List files that have no findings as well
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Print the summary without the findings
.TP
\fB\-\-timings\fR
Print how long each stage of the scan took, and what it did
.TP
\fB\-\-stats\fR
Counts only: which rules and families fired, and how often
.TP
\fB\-\-group\-by\fR \fI<GROUPING>\fR [default: file]
What the listing is a list of
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
file
.IP \(bu 2
rule
.IP \(bu 2
family
.IP \(bu 2
severity
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-sort\fR \fI<ORDER>\fR [default: line]
What decides the order inside each group
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
line
.IP \(bu 2
severity
.IP \(bu 2
file
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-top\fR \fI<N>\fR
List only this many groups; the rest are counted
.TP
\fB\-\-show\-suppressed\fR
List the findings a comment waives, alongside the ones it does not
.TP
\fB\-\-context\fR \fI<N>\fR
Lines of code shown either side of a finding. Two under `\-\-detail full`, none otherwise, unless this says
.TP
\fB\-\-detail\fR \fI<DETAIL>\fR [default: normal]
How much of each finding to print
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
terse: One line per finding
.IP \(bu 2
normal: The reason once per rule, the cost once per file
.IP \(bu 2
full: Every line on every finding
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-reporter\fR \fI<NAME[=PATH]>\fR
Where a report goes: `<name>` for stdout, `<name>=<path>` for a file; repeatable
.SH GATE
.TP
\fB\-\-fail\-on\fR \fI<FAIL_ON>\fR
Lowest severity that fails the run
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
info
.IP \(bu 2
warning
.IP \(bu 2
error
.IP \(bu 2
never
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-findings\fR \fI<ALLOW_FINDINGS>\fR
Findings allowed before the run fails
.TP
\fB\-\-min\-health\fR \fI<MIN_HEALTH>\fR
Health score below which the run fails; 0 disables
.TP
\fB\-\-min\-grade\fR \fI<MIN_GRADE>\fR
Lowest grade any single file may carry
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
pristine
.IP \(bu 2
clean
.IP \(bu 2
fair
.IP \(bu 2
poor
.IP \(bu 2
critical
.IP \(bu 2
never
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-fail\-on\-incomplete\fR
Fail when a design pattern is half applied
.SH EXTRA
Examples:
  rqx check \-\-base main               review the branch against main
  rqx check \-\-base main \-\-fail\-on error
                                      and fail CI on any error
  rqx check \-\-fix \-w                  apply the proven fixes first
